'''''Spirodela punctata''''' (or '''''Landoltia punctata''''', common name '''dotted duckweed'''<ref>{{PLANTS|id=LAPU12|taxon=Landoltia punctata|accessdate=30 May 2015}}</ref>) is a species of [[duckweed]] ([[Lemnoideae]]).  The species is morphologically intermediate between ''[[Lemna]]'' and other species of ''[[Spirodela]]''.  In 1999 D.H. Les and D.J. Crawford proposed segregating the species to a new genus '''''Landoltia''''' containing just the species ''L.&nbsp;punctata'', on the basis of biochemical and DNA studies.

''S. punctata'' originally was found in Australia and South Asia, but today it can also be found in the Southern and Eastern United States.

